        "response": "I'll provide a simple explanation of photosynthesis.\n\n## What is photosynthesis?\n\nPhotosynthesis is how **plants make their own food**, using sunlight, water, and air.\n\n### The simple recipe:\n\n**Ingredients:**\n- ☀️ Sunlight\n- 💧 Water (from the roots)\n- 🌬️ Carbon dioxide (from the air)\n\n**Result:**\n- 🍬 Sugar/glucose (the plant's food)\n- 💨 Oxygen (released into the air)\n\n### How it works — step by step:\n\n1. **Absorb sunlight** — Leaves have a green pigment called chlorophyll (that's what makes plants green) that captures energy from sunlight.\n2. **Take in water** — Roots pull water up from the soil into the leaves.\n3. **Breathe in air** — Tiny openings on leaves (stomata) take in carbon dioxide from the air.\n4. **Convert to food** — The sunlight energy combines water and carbon dioxide to make sugar.\n5. **Release oxygen** — Oxygen is given off as a byproduct.\n\n### Why it matters to us:\n\n- Plants get their energy from the sugar they make.\n- **We get oxygen** — nearly all the oxygen in the air comes from photosynthesis.\n- It's the **base of the food chain** — almost all food energy on Earth traces back to this process.\n- It also helps absorb carbon dioxide from the atmosphere.\n\n### One-line summary:\nPlants turn sunlight, water, and carbon dioxide into food (sugar) and oxygen — and in doing so, they feed nearly all life on Earth.",
